Root cause:
The bug was caused by the bss section being cleared before ensuring that the initrd (initial ramdisk) was moved to a safe location. During the decompression process, the bss section could overlap with the initrd, leading to corruption of the initrd contents. The patch reorders the operations to first move the initrd and then clear the bss section, preventing any potential overlap and corruption. Additionally, the patch corrects the logic for checking overlaps with the parameter block by using the correct initrd size.
